WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:07.439
On November 13th, gunmen and bombers attacked
a number of locations throughout Paris.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:11.900
They killed over 120 people, and wounded an
even larger number.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.570
ISIS, otherwise known as the Islamic State,
claimed responsibility for these attacks.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:28.849
[A group of believers from the Soldiers of
the Caliphate, set out targeting the capitol

00:00:28.849 --> 00:00:34.260
of prostitution and vice -- the lead carrier
of the cross in Europe, Paris.]

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.489
In the past, ISIS hasn't really launched any
major terrorist attacks abroad.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:43.710
ISIS's basic goal is holding on to its territory
in Iraq and Syria. Why change your strategy

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.969
now?

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:49.399
One theory, according to the Brooking Institute's
Will McCants, is that they are trying to warn

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:55.989
off their enemies abroad.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:01:00.819
Recently ISIS has been losing territory. Bombing
from the US-led coalition, which includes

00:01:00.819 --> 00:01:04.370
France, has hurt the group.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:07.820
[They have lost something like 25 percent
of their territory.]

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.380
So ISIS has a problem: it has strong foreign
militaries fighting against it, and it doesn't

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.260
have a good way to attack back at them.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.860
So one theory according to McCants, is that
this attack is a means of showing these enemies

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:21.340
that ISIS will hurt them if they keep attacking
them.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:26.290
Evidence for this theory includes the fact
that ISIS recently a part of Lebanon that's

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:27.780
a Hezbollah stronghold.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:33.050
Hezbollah is a Lebanese militia that is fighting
on the same side as Bashar al-Assad in Syria,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.810
nominally an ISIS enemy

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:39.820
Similarly there is strong suspicion that Syria
bombed a Russian airliner in Egypt.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:45.630
So the idea here is that ISIS wants to show
that you will pay a price if you attack ISIS

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.100
in Syria and Iraq.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.500
So ISIS's attack in Paris might not have been
out of strength. It might have been out of

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:51.880
weakness.

